  "id": "belief-in-a-just-world",
  "term": "belief in a just world",
  "definition": "Belief in a just world is the tendency to see the world as fair and to think that people generally get what they deserve. In psychology, it is described as a relatively stable personal trait with adaptive coping functions and has been linked to better well-being and lower distress.",
